// microbench hop1_edgefilter: the knows EDGES of a person, both directions, created before
// 2011-01-01 (T5, edge-property filter). Counts edges, not distinct neighbors, as the
// evaluator does (no dedup step).
// Reads: the knows edge index (both sides), then each edge's creationDate (in the edge document).
// Evaluator: queries/hop.py hop1_edgefilter -- read_neighbors(edge_props=[creationDate]) +
// filter creationDate < DATE_CUTOFF (1293840000000), count-final.
// mb2 lineage: MB35-36, 27-28 (MB35 = OUTBOUND with a date window on e.creationDate).
FOR v, e IN 1..1 ANY CONCAT("Person/", @personId) knows
    FILTER e.creationDate < 1293840000000
    RETURN e._key
